#
# --- X1: Policy ---
# scripture: A prudent man concealeth knowledge — Proverbs 12:23
# never:
#   - Commit real secrets, API keys, or passwords
#   - Use weak/guessable secret values in production
#   - Share .env files via insecure channels
#   - Log environment variables in production
#   - Remove 3-block documentation structure
# careful:
#   - Changing variable names (breaks code references)
#   - Removing variables (may break dependent code)
#   - Changing production defaults
# safe:
#   - Add new environment variables
#   - Change default development values
#   - Add comments explaining variables
#   - Reorganize sections for clarity
#
# --- X4: Reference ---
# related_files:
#   - gitignore.gitignore — must exclude .env files (co-located)
#   - editorconfig.editorconfig — co-located editor config
#   - template.mk — co-located build system template
# validate: source .env && echo $APP_NAME
# creating_env_example:
#   Replace real values with placeholders: DB_PASSWORD=[your-database-password]
#   The .env.example file IS committed to version control.
#   New developers copy it to .env and fill in real values.
#
# --- X5: Note ---
# note:      Environment files configure application behavior and store secrets.
#            Proper handling of these values is a matter of stewardship and trust.
# scripture: A prudent man concealeth knowledge — Proverbs 12:23
# anchor:    Genesis 1:1 anchors everything
#
# --- X6: Template ---
# usage:     cp env.env .env -> update values -> configure gitignore
# update:
#   - Add project-specific variables to Co section
#   - Update M1 key and title for project
#   - Update M2 dates
#   - Add project-specific categories
# after:
#   - Ensure .env is in .gitignore
#   - Create .env.example with placeholder values
#   - Remove X6 section
#
